    MIT

tree-sitter-rust.wasm
    compiled from tree-sitter-rust@0.20.4
    (https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust)
    Copyright (c) 2017 Maxim Sokolov
    MIT

tree-sitter-java.wasm
    compiled from tree-sitter-java@0.20.2
    (https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-java)
    Copyright (c) 2017 Ayman Nadeem
    MIT

The four grammar binaries were compiled by tree-sitter-wasms@0.1.13
(https://github.com/Gregoor/tree-sitter-wasms). That packaging layer is released
into the public domain under the Unlicense and imposes no conditions of its own —
but it cannot relicense the grammars it compiled, which is why their MIT notices
appear above. The grammar versions are the ones that package pins for the build
(`^0.20.3`, `^0.21.0`, `^0.20.4`, `^0.20.2`); the copyright lines do not change
within those ranges.

Note that all four grammars have DIFFERENT copyright holders. That is why none of
these lines was written from memory.

